course: dictionary
lesson: 15760
title: Troublemaker
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A troublemaker is a person who often causes problems. Look at the two parts of the word: trouble means problems or bother, and a maker is someone who makes something. «Ben is a real troublemaker, so the teacher moved him to the front.» The word trouble in the sentence is your first clue.
explain: Troublemakers break rules, start fights or upset others on purpose. «Ben is a bit of a troublemaker, but he helped carry the books.» The word «but» is a clue that the story is not only about bad behaviour. Stories often show that a troublemaker has reasons, or can change.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «Ben is a real person who often causes problems, so the teacher moved him.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Troublemaker is a noun: a troublemaker, troublemakers.
fact: «Troublemaker» means a person who often causes problems, for example by breaking rules, starting fights or upsetting others on purpose.
fact: Common phrases are «a real troublemaker», «a bit of a troublemaker» and «known as a troublemaker».
fact: The word is built from two smaller words: trouble and maker.
fact: Stories often show that a troublemaker has reasons, or can change.
exercise: «Mia is known as a troublemaker because she starts arguments in class.» What is a troublemaker? | *A person who often causes problems | A person who sings well | A person who wins every race | A person who helps everyone tidy up
exercise: «Sam is a bit of a troublemaker, but he helped the teacher carry the books.» What does «a bit of a troublemaker» suggest? | Sam never does anything wrong | Sam is very tall | Sam is the teacher | *Sam sometimes causes problems
exercise: Which two smaller words make up troublemaker? | trouble and maid | *trouble and maker | tro andublemaker | trouble and mate
test: The teacher moved the troublemaker to the front of the class. Why might a teacher do this? | To give them a prize | *So they can be watched and cause fewer problems | To let them sleep | To hide them from the class
test: Which best describes a troublemaker? | A person who is always quiet and shy | A person who lives in a castle | A person who runs very fast | *A person who often causes problems or breaks rules
exam: Ben is a troublemaker at the start of a story, but by the end he helps his friends. What does this show? | *Stories can show that a troublemaker can change | Ben is invisible | Ben is a teacher | Ben will always cause trouble
